    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d433">

                <pb facs="0448" n="358" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg358"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2675</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4278</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-08-27"><hi rendition="#italic">August 27, 1918</hi></date>.
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 12.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my cipher telegram No.
                    4434 of August 22,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d433-f1"/> transmitting a <hi
                        rendition="#italic">résumé</hi> of the despatches handed me by the
                    representative <pb facs="0449" n="359" xml:id="pg359"/> of the Russian Soviet
                    government in Switzerland, I have the honor to transmit herewith translations in
                    full of these three despatches.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d433-f2"/></p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pleasant A.
                                Stovall</hi></signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d433-a1.xml" xpointer="d433-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d433-f1" n="1" xml:id="d433-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d433-f2" n="1" xml:id="d433-f2-content">
                <p>Two enclosures, not printed, outlined conditions under which representatives and
                    citizens of countries of the Entente might leave Russia. One was addressed to
                    the Netherland Minister at Petrograd; the second bore no designation.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
